g his piano skills. He taught himself to play the piano by ear at age ten. A generous piano tuner gifted him a valuable instrument and professional lessons. His album features diverse musical styles, including jazz and gospel influences. This release marks a significant milestone in his developing musical career.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-teen-jude-kofie-taught-himself-piano-by-ear-at-10-a-stranger-bought-him-a-15000-grand-piano-and-now-he-has-released-his-debut-album/articleshow/133050467.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/colorado-teen-jude-kofie-taught-himself-piano-by-ear-at-10-a-stranger-bought-him-a-15000-grand-piano-and-now-he-has-released-his-debut-album/articleshow/133050467.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T15:59:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133050636,imgsize-103544.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Greenland issues ‘strong warning’ over Arctic drilling by Trump-linked firm]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133050012.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A US oil firm has moved equipment to Greenland without local approval. This action occurs while President Trump seeks greater US influence over the territory. Greenland's government issued a strong warning regarding the unauthorized logistical operation. The company plans to drill for oil, which faces environmental and political questions. The situation highlights Greenland's resource development authority amid US strategic interests.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/greenland-issues-strong-warning-as-trump-linked-us-oil-firm-pushes-ahead-with-arctic-drilling/articleshow/133050012.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/greenland-issues-strong-warning-as-trump-linked-us-oil-firm-pushes-ahead-with-arctic-drilling/articleshow/133050012.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T15:25:35+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Yashasvi Vasistha</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133050045,imgsize-319602.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[10-year-old baker's grand champion cake fetches $15,000 at Maryland county fair auction]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133049506.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[At a recent county fair auction, a remarkable cake created by 10-year-old baker Herbie Martin IV fetched an astounding $15,000. Herbie dedicated countless late-night hours to master his delightful lemon blueberry recipe. This impressive sale contributed to an overall fundraising goal, raising more than $100,000 for upcoming fairs and youth initiatives, with Herbie's cake standing out as the highlight of the event.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/food-news/maryland-10-year-old-herbie-martin-iv-stayed-up-until-2-a-m-perfecting-his-lemon-blueberry-buttercream-cake-the-grand-champion-cake-sold-for-15000/articleshow/133049506.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/life-style/food-news/maryland-10-year-old-herbie-martin-iv-stayed-up-until-2-a-m-perfecting-his-lemon-blueberry-buttercream-cake-the-grand-champion-cake-sold-for-15000/articleshow/133049506.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T14:33:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133049590,imgsize-1351488.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[56 decomposing bodies found at Chicago funeral home; owner’s licence suspended]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133050533.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/56-decomposing-bodies-found-at-chicago-funeral-home-owners-licence-suspended/articleshow/133050533.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/56-decomposing-bodies-found-at-chicago-funeral-home-owners-licence-suspended/articleshow/133050533.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T16:10:57+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133050794,imgsize-147848.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Senate passes stopgap funding bill to avert shutdown ahead of midterms]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133049620.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[In a decisive move, the US Senate has passed a temporary spending bill aimed at funding government operations until December eleventh. This crucial legislation is designed to avert a government shutdown just before the midterm elections. Key components of the bill address border patrol funding as requested by Democrats and extend the deadline for enforcing a federal prohibition on certain hemp products by a month.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-senate-passes-stopgap-funding-bill-to-avert-shutdown-ahead-of-midterms/articleshow/133049620.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/us-senate-passes-stopgap-funding-bill-to-avert-shutdown-ahead-of-midterms/articleshow/133049620.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T14:56:36+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133049834,imgsize-190534.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Green Bank Radio Restrictions: Tiny US town lives under radio-silence laws]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133048642.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/inside-the-us-town-where-cell-phones-barely-work-because-scientists-are-listening-to-the-universe/articleshow/133048642.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/inside-the-us-town-where-cell-phones-barely-work-because-scientists-are-listening-to-the-universe/articleshow/133048642.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T14:31:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133049596,imgsize-2011296.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Spain's blood-red Río Tinto may hold clues to life on Mars, Nasa says]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133048345.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The Río Tinto in Spain captivates with its vivid red and orange colors, a result of both its ancient geology and extensive mining activities. In this caustic environment, specialized microorganisms flourish by harnessing energy from iron and sulfur compounds. Over millennia, mining has intensified these natural chemical reactions, further enhancing the river’s striking look. NASA's interest lies in finding similar minerals to explore potential Martian life.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/spains-blood-red-ro-tinto-river-is-as-acidic-as-vinegar-and-nasa-says-it-could-help-scientists-find-life-on-mars/articleshow/133048345.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/spains-blood-red-ro-tinto-river-is-as-acidic-as-vinegar-and-nasa-says-it-could-help-scientists-find-life-on-mars/articleshow/133048345.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T12:48:26+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133048382,imgsize-153419.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Kinshasa Growth Deepens Poverty: World Bank data tracks soaring population]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133048505.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/kinshasa-is-growing-faster-than-almost-any-city-in-africa-but-its-population-boom-is-not-making-people-richer/articleshow/133048505.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/kinshasa-is-growing-faster-than-almost-any-city-in-africa-but-its-population-boom-is-not-making-people-richer/articleshow/133048505.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T13:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133048539,imgsize-228916.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[China’s hanging coffins had no known builders. Ancient DNA points to Bo people]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133048355.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/for-centuries-chinas-hanging-coffins-had-no-known-builders-ancient-dna-now-points-to-the-bo-people/articleshow/133048355.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/china/for-centuries-chinas-hanging-coffins-had-no-known-builders-ancient-dna-now-points-to-the-bo-people/articleshow/133048355.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T13:07:22+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133048500,imgsize-222772.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US Fire Service In Antarctica: Frozen desert fuels fire risk]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133048644.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/antarctica-is-covered-in-ice-yet-its-dry-desert-climate-makes-fire-so-dangerous-that-the-us-maintains-a-full-time-professional-fire-department/articleshow/133048644.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/antarctica-is-covered-in-ice-yet-its-dry-desert-climate-makes-fire-so-dangerous-that-the-us-maintains-a-full-time-professional-fire-department/articleshow/133048644.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-08T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133048745,imgsize-88264.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[US officials will not release cool water from Glen Canyon Dam this year, protecting hydropower while threatening humpback chub]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133049127.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[This year, federal officials have decided against releasing cool water from the Colorado River reservoirs, emphasizing the need for hydropower production over the conservation of a threatened fish species. The river and its reservoirs are facing severe depletion from overuse and climate change, while states have been unable to reach a long-term agreement on water sha